※ pl4g-test: compile=error
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4627 LANG_HANDED_OUT_NOT_MADE

※ `→ T in pool`, with `pool` no parameter, says the body makes `pool` -- in its own scope, before any
※ way out that answers.  Made inside the arm of an `if`, there is a way out that never makes it.

fn named(n: u64) → str in pool:
    if n = 0u64:
        let pool: mut arena = ⎕arena
        return "a" ⧺ "b" in pool
    "c"

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let s: str in k = named(1u64)
    defer ⎕empty(k)
    if s = "c": 0u6 else: 1u6
